# Compound components

Presentational primitives under `components/` and `@pond/ui` export one PascalCase object. Call sites read as a sentence (`Settings.Page`, `Dialog.Title`).

## Do

```tsx
type TitleProps = React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<"h1">;

function Title({ className, ...props }: TitleProps) {
  return <h1 className={cn(styles.title, className)} {...props} />;
}

export const Settings = { Page, Header, Title };
```

- Props extend the element they render via `React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<"tag">`.
- Destructure custom props, spread `...props` last.
- Merge `className` with `import { clsx as cn } from "clsx"`.
- Variants are a string union forwarded as `data-*`. No boolean prop walls, no `as` prop.
- Named export only. No default export.

## Don't

```tsx
export { Page, Header, Title };
export default function Card() {}
```

A single-element wrapper with no parts (`Button`, `Spinner`) may be one named function. Pages, hooks, and main-process code are not compounds.

Reference: `packages/ui/src/settings`, `packages/ui/src/dialog`.
